<small>A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> LORD, how are they increased that trouble me! many <i>are</i> they that rise up against me.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Many <i>there be</i> which say of my soul, <i>There is</i> no help for him in God. Selah.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> But thou, O LORD, <i>art</i> a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> I cried unto the LORD with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy hill. Selah.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustained me.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, that have set <i>themselves</i> against me round about.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies <i>upon</i> the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the ungodly.<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> Salvation <i>belongeth</i> unto the LORD: thy blessing <i>is</i> upon thy people. Selah. <br />
